Subject: [PATCH] game: make the main-menu work area a real object under
 SDK_PORT_3DS

The DS build lays the main menu work area out as a run of adjacent bss
globals (gMainMenuUtilCryptoHeapId, gMainMenuUtilWork,
gMainMenuUtilSprites, ...) and the code aliases it with
&gMainMenuUtilCryptoHeapId + 1. The port gives every global its own
section, so that pointer no longer names the work area; gMainMenuUtilWork
was also declared as 13 words while MainMenuUtilWork is several kilobytes.
The fade state written by MainMenuUtil_StartFade landed somewhere else, so
WaitFade always saw nextState 0 and the main menu re-ran its graphics setup
every frame until the heap ran out (a crash in MIi_CpuClear16 with a NULL
buffer).

Under SDK_PORT_3DS, make gMainMenuUtilWork the real MainMenuUtilWork
object, take its address everywhere the code used the adjacency trick, and
point the sprite list at work->sprites. The DS text is under #else and
unchanged: gcc-10 -E -P without SDK_PORT_3DS is byte-identical for both
files (0 diff lines).

